Why added:
- Firewalls: filter traffic and protect servers
- SSL: encrypt communication (HTTPS)
- Monitoring: track performance and detect issues

Firewalls:
Control allowed/blocked traffic

HTTPS:
Encrypts data between user and server

Monitoring:
Detect errors, performance issues

Data collection:
Agent on each server sends metrics/logs

QPS monitoring:
Use Nginx logs or metrics to measure requests per second

Issues:

- SSL termination:
Traffic between LB and servers not encrypted

- One writable DB:
Primary is bottleneck and SPOF for writes

- Same components:
Hard to scale, resource conflicts
